{"title":"Teaching","markdown":{"yaml":{"title":"Teaching","toc":false},"headingText":"Tutoring","containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"about-heading-rule\"></div>\n```\n\nI find that explaining mathematics to others sharpens my own understanding\nmore than almost anything else. I have been tutoring since [year], working\nwith students one-on-one at both the high school and undergraduate level.\n\n---\n\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"tutor-card\">\n  <div class=\"tutor-icon\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke-width=\"1.8\">\n      <path d=\"M12 14l9-5-9-5-9 5 9 5z\"/>\n      <path d=\"M12 14l6.16-3.422A12.08 12.08 0 0 1 18 18a12.08 12.08 0 0 1-6 1 12.08 12.08 0 0 1-6-1 12.08 12.08 0 0 1-.16-7.422L12 14z\"/>\n    </svg>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-level\">University</div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-title\">Undergraduate Tutoring — York University</div>\n    <p class=\"tutor-body\">\n      One-on-one tutoring for undergraduate students at York University,\n      helping them build both procedural fluency and genuine conceptual\n      understanding. I focus on working through problems together rather\n      than simply demonstrating solutions.\n    </p>\n    <div class=\"tutor-subjects\">\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Calculus I &amp; II</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Linear Algebra</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Real Analysis</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">[Add your subjects]</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"tutor-card\">\n  <div class=\"tutor-icon\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke-width=\"1.8\">\n      <path d=\"M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z\"/>\n      <path d=\"M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z\"/>\n    </svg>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-level\">High School</div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-title\">Private Tutoring</div>\n    <p class=\"tutor-body\">\n      One-on-one tutoring for high school students, covering the full\n      curriculum through to final-year and pre-university level. I pay\n      particular attention to students who feel they \"just aren't math\n      people\" — in my experience, the issue is almost never ability.\n    </p>\n    <div class=\"tutor-subjects\">\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Algebra</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Precalculus</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Calculus</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Statistics</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">[Add your subjects]</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Teaching philosophy\n\nI believe the goal of mathematical education is not to produce students\nwho can execute procedures, but students who can *think* — who can sit\nwith a problem they have never seen before and find a way in. In\npractice, this means I spend a lot of time asking questions rather than\ngiving answers, and encouraging students to articulate why a method works\nrather than just that it works.\n\nI am always happy to hear from students looking for support.\nFeel free to [get in touch](about.qmd).\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":"\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"about-heading-rule\"></div>\n```\n\nI find that explaining mathematics to others sharpens my own understanding\nmore than almost anything else. I have been tutoring since [year], working\nwith students one-on-one at both the high school and undergraduate level.\n\n---\n\n## Tutoring\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"tutor-card\">\n  <div class=\"tutor-icon\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke-width=\"1.8\">\n      <path d=\"M12 14l9-5-9-5-9 5 9 5z\"/>\n      <path d=\"M12 14l6.16-3.422A12.08 12.08 0 0 1 18 18a12.08 12.08 0 0 1-6 1 12.08 12.08 0 0 1-6-1 12.08 12.08 0 0 1-.16-7.422L12 14z\"/>\n    </svg>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-level\">University</div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-title\">Undergraduate Tutoring — York University</div>\n    <p class=\"tutor-body\">\n      One-on-one tutoring for undergraduate students at York University,\n      helping them build both procedural fluency and genuine conceptual\n      understanding. I focus on working through problems together rather\n      than simply demonstrating solutions.\n    </p>\n    <div class=\"tutor-subjects\">\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Calculus I &amp; II</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Linear Algebra</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Real Analysis</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">[Add your subjects]</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"tutor-card\">\n  <div class=\"tutor-icon\">\n    <svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" stroke-width=\"1.8\">\n      <path d=\"M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z\"/>\n      <path d=\"M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z\"/>\n    </svg>\n  </div>\n  <div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-level\">High School</div>\n    <div class=\"tutor-title\">Private Tutoring</div>\n    <p class=\"tutor-body\">\n      One-on-one tutoring for high school students, covering the full\n      curriculum through to final-year and pre-university level. I pay\n      particular attention to students who feel they \"just aren't math\n      people\" — in my experience, the issue is almost never ability.\n    </p>\n    <div class=\"tutor-subjects\">\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Algebra</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Precalculus</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Calculus</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">Statistics</span>\n      <span class=\"tutor-tag\">[Add your subjects]</span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n---\n\n## Teaching philosophy\n\nI believe the goal of mathematical education is not to produce students\nwho can execute procedures, but students who can *think* — who can sit\nwith a problem they have never seen before and find a way in. In\npractice, this means I spend a lot of time asking questions rather than\ngiving answers, and encouraging students to articulate why a method works\nrather than just that it works.\n\nI am always happy to hear from students looking for support.\nFeel free to [get in touch](about.qmd).\n"},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":"auto","echo":true,"output":true,"warning":false,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":true,"code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":true,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex":"makeindex","latex-makeindex-opts":[],"latex-tlmgr-opts":[],"latex-input-paths":[],"latex-output-dir":null,"link-external-icon":false,"link-external-newwindow":true,"self-contained-math":false,"format-resources":[],"notebook-links":true},"pandoc":{"standalone":true,"wrap":"none","default-image-extension":"png","to":"html","css":["styles.css"],"toc":false,"toc-depth":3,"output-file":"teaching.html"},"language":{"toc-title-document":"Table of contents","toc-title-website":"On this page","related-formats-title":"Other Formats","related-notebooks-title":"Notebooks","source-notebooks-prefix":"Source","other-links-title":"Other Links","code-links-title":"Code Links","launch-dev-container-title":"Launch Dev Container","launch-binder-title":"Launch Binder","article-notebook-label":"Article Notebook","notebook-preview-download":"Download Notebook","notebook-preview-download-src":"Download Source","notebook-preview-ba